## Why This Is Asked
Tests CGO struct mappings, error handling, and concurrency in a beginner-friendly way. It targets memory ownership and cross-language data layout without exposing advanced ownership tricks.

## Key Concepts
- Go<->C struct translation
- CGO error handling and return codes
- Concurrency with worker pools and channel coordination

## Code Example
```c
// C header
typedef struct { int a; double b; } Config;
typedef struct { int sum; double product; } Result;
int compute(const Config* cfg, Result* out);
```
```c
// Minimal implementation (compile as C file)
#include <math.h>
int compute(const Config* cfg, Result* out) {
  if (!cfg || !out) return -1;
  out->sum = cfg->a + (int)cfg->b;
  out->product = cfg->a * cfg->b;
  return 0;
}
```

